{"schema": "workere-benchmark-suite/v1", "protocol": "workere-historical-relations/v1", "config": {"seed": 42, "active_dataset": "causal_timebank", "datasets": {"causal_timebank": {"name": "CausalTimeBank-standard-eci", "repo_id": "Nofing/CausalTimeBank-standard-eci-workere", "split": "train", "text_field": "text", "ann_field": "annots", "max_examples": 0, "kfold": {"enabled": true, "n_folds": 10}, "constrain_to_pair_list": false}}, "data": {"shuffle_docs": true, "shuffle_pair_list": true, "reshuffle_per_resample": true, "binary_undirected": false, "vote_to_binary": false, "binary_default": "norel", "novote_norel": true, "labels": ["causes", "causedby", "norel"]}, "experiment": {"resampling": {"enabled": true, "n_runs": 7, "tie_breaking": "norel", "distinct_fewshots": true}}}, "documents": [{"id": "wsj_0585", "idx": 118, "text": "Market makers in Nasdaq over-the-counter stocks are <ei1 adding> their voices to the swelling chorus of complaints about program trading . Their motivation , however , has a strong practical aspect : Program trading is hazardous to their paychecks . The most controversial form of program trading , stock-index <ei2 arbitrage> , is \" <ei3 making> it <ei4 tough> for traders to make money , \" <ei5 declares> Robert Antolini , head of OTC trading at Donaldson , Lufkin amp Jenrette . Stock-index <ei6 arbitrage> -- the computer-guided buying and selling of stocks with offsetting trades in stock-index futures to profit from fleeting price discrepancies -- <ei7 affects> the OTC market directly through the 31 stocks included in Standard amp Poor 's 500-stock index . The SampP 500 is often used in arbitrage strategies . The portion of OTC volume attributable to program trading is n't known , as it is on the New York Stock Exchange , where it <ei8 amounted> to more than 13 % in September . <ei10 Estimates> from traders put it at less than 5 % of Nasdaq 's average daily volume of roughly 133 million shares . Other market-maker gripes : Program <ei11 trading> also <ei12 causes> the Nasdaq Composite Index to <ei13 lose> ground against other segments of the stock market . Because of program <ei15 trading> it is more <ei16 difficult> to <ei17 trade> many OTC stocks without sharp price <ei18 moves> , a condition known as illiquidity . Moreover , the price <ei19 volatility> that is <ei20 amplified> by program <ei22 trading> is <ei23 undercutting> <ei24 efforts> to <ei25 woo> individual investors back to an OTC market that sorely <ei26 misses> them . Some of these <ei27 problems> are neither new nor unique to the OTC market . But the big , often tumultuous <ei28 slide> in stock prices this month has <ei30 turned> some of those who have been <ei31 profiting> from the practice against it . Peter DaPuzzo , head of retail equity trading at Shearson Lehman Hutton , <ei32 acknowledges> that he was n't <ei33 troubled> by program <ei34 trading> when it <ei35 began> in the pre-crash bull market because it <ei37 added> liquidity and people were <ei38 pleased> to <ei39 see> stock prices <ei40 rising> . \" We were n't as concerned until they <ei41 became> sell programs , \" <ei42 says> Mr. DaPuzzo , who now <ei44 thinks> it <ei45 adds> unnecessary volatility . Shearson Lehman , however , executes program trades for clients . Merrill Lynch , Goldman Sachs and Kidder Peabody , in addition to Shearson , do program-trade OTC stocks . Shearson , Merrill Lynch and Goldman Sachs say they do so only for customers , however . Kidder Peabody does program trading for its own as well as clients ' accounts . Of course , there were sell <ei46 programs> in past years , too , but they <ei48 seem> to <ei49 hurt> market makers more painfully these days . That 's largely because of defensive <ei52 measures> they <ei53 adopted> after the 1987 <ei55 crash> , when individual investors <ei56 fled> the market and trading activity <ei57 dwindled> . Market makers , to <ei58 cut> costs , <ei59 slashed> inventories of stocks they keep on hand to sell investors when other holders are n't selling . And to <ei60 protect> their reduced capital investment from <ei61 eroding> further , market makers <ei62 became> quicker to <ei63 lower> price quotes when sell programs are <ei64 in> progress . On days when prices are tumbling , they must be <ei65 willing> to <ei66 buy> shares from sellers when no one else will . In such an environment , market makers can <ei67 suffer> huge <ei68 losses> both on trades made that day at steadily dropping prices and in the value of their inventories of shares . \" It <ei69 makes> no <ei70 sense> for us to <ei71 put> money at risk when you <ei72 know> you 're going to lose , \" <ei73 says> Mr. Antolini , of Donaldson Lufkin . But this <ei74 skittishness> , Mr. Antolini says , is <ei75 creating> liquidity <ei76 problems> in certain OTC stocks . \" It 's <ei77 harder> to sell stocks when the sell programs come in because some market makers do n't <ei79 want> to { take the orders } . No one has big positions and no one wants to take big risks . \" Joseph Hardiman , president of the National Association of Securities Dealers , which oversees trading on Nasdaq , <ei80 agrees> that program trading is <ei81 hurting> the market 's <ei82 efforts> to <ei83 bring> back small investors . But , he <ei84 observes> , while makers <ei85 suffer> <ei86 losses> when program trading <ei87 drags> the market down , they also <ei88 make> money when program trading <ei89 pushes> the prices higher . \" Sometimes { traders } <ei90 lose> sight of that , \" he <ei91 says> . The OTC stocks in the SampP 500 include Nasdaq 's biggest , such as Apple Computer , MCI Communications , Tele - Communications and Liz Claiborne . These big stocks greatly influence the Nasdaq Composite Index . When the computers say \" sell , \" the composite tumbles as well as the Dow Jones Industrial Average . The problem , market makers say , is that while the industrial average and the SampP 500 usually recover as buy programs kick in , the Nasdaq Composite frequently is left behind . Eight trading days after Oct . 12 , the day before the stock market <ei95 plunge> , for instance , the Nasdaq Composite had <ei96 fallen> 4.3 % , compared with 3.3 % for the SampP 500 , 3.5 % for the New York Stock Exchange Composite Index and 3.6 % for the industrial average . This gap eventually <ei97 closes> , but slowly . Three days later , as of Friday 's <ei100 close> , the Nasdaq Composite was down 6 % , compared with 5.9 % for the industrial average , 5.7 % for the SampP 500 and 5.8 % for the Big Board Composite . The main reason for this <ei102 lag> is that individual investors <ei103 own> 65 % of the OTC market 's capitalization , <ei104 according> to Mr. Hardiman , much more than on the Big Board . Such investors tend to be more cautious than institutional investors are about re-entering the market after massive selloffs , market makers say . The Nasdaq Composite Index <ei105 tumbled> 5.39 , or 1.2 % to 452.76 on Friday . For the week , the index <ei108 dropped> 3.8 % . <ei109 Weakness> in big technology stocks <ei110 hurt> the composite as well as the Nasdaq 100 Index , which <ei111 fell> 1.4 % , or 6.43 , on Friday , to 437.68 . The Nasdaq Financial Index <ei113 lost> about 1 % , or 3.95 , to 448.80 . Friday 's trading volume <ei115 totaled> 132.8 million shares . The average daily share turnover for October is almost 148 million shares . LIN Broadcasting <ei117 surged> 4 5/8 to 112 5/8 ; LIN and BellSouth <ei118 sweetened> their merger agreement in an <ei119 attempt> to <ei120 keep> shareholders from <ei121 tendering> their shares to McCaw Cellular Communications . McCaw , which <ei122 dropped> 2 1/2 to 37 3/4 , has <ei123 offered> $ 125 a share for a majority of LIN 's shares . The revised LIN - BellSouth agreement <ei124 boosts> the dollar amount of the special dividend LIN promises to pay shareholders . LIN now <ei126 plans> to <ei127 dole> out $ 42 a share in cash , up from the earlier $ 20 amount . Intel <ei128 eased> 1/8 to 31 7/8 . The semiconductor concern <ei129 said> the <ei130 interruption> in <ei131 shipment> of its 80486 computer chip will be <ei132 brief> and <ei133 have> little <ei134 impact> on the company 's earnings . The stock <ei135 fell> 7/8 Thursday amid <ei137 concerns> over problems discovered with the chip . Intel <ei138 told> analysts that the company will <ei139 resume> <ei140 shipments> of the chips within two to three weeks . Weisfield 's <ei142 rocketed> 9 1/2 to 39 after the jewelry store operator <ei143 said> it is in preliminary <ei144 discussions> , with a party it would n't <ei145 identify> , regarding the possible <ei146 acquisition> of the company . Starpointe Savings Bank <ei147 rose> 3 to 20 after the Federal Deposit Insurance Corp. <ei148 approved> Dime Savings Bank of New York 's $ 21-a-share <ei149 acquisition> of Starpointe . Kirschner Medical <ei150 fell> 4 to 15 . The company <ei151 said> its third-quarter earnings will probably be <ei153 lower> than the 16 cents a share it <ei154 reported> last year , despite a <ei156 rise> in the company 's revenue . Kirschner <ei157 earned> $ 376,000 on revenue of $ 14.5 million in the 1988 quarter . The company <ei159 blamed> a number of factors for the earnings <ei160 decline> , including softer <ei161 sales> of joint-implants .", "gold": [["ei2", "causes", "ei4"], ["ei11", "causes", "ei13"], ["ei15", "causes", "ei16"], ["ei22", "causes", "ei20"], ["ei37", "causes", "ei33"], ["ei38", "causes", "ei33"], ["ei62", "causes", "ei61"], ["ei79", "causes", "ei77"], ["ei103", "causes", "ei102"], ["ei118", "causes", "ei121"], ["ei4", "causedby", "ei2"], ["ei13", "causedby", "ei11"], ["ei16", "causedby", "ei15"], ["ei20", "causedby", "ei22"], ["ei33", "causedby", "ei37"], ["ei33", "causedby", "ei38"], ["ei61", "causedby", "ei62"], ["ei77", "causedby", "ei79"], ["ei102", "causedby", "ei103"], ["ei121", "causedby", "ei118"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8"